WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.834
Here it is running.

2
00:00:01.664 --> 00:00:03.464
The customer types what's going on.

3
00:00:03.818 --> 00:00:07.929
Married in the spring, a baby, renting, hoping to buy next year.

4
00:00:08.354 --> 00:00:10.038
Saoirse doesn't reach for a product.

5
00:00:10.418 --> 00:00:14.999
It asks one question, then records what it learns, where each fact came from.

6
00:00:15.404 --> 00:00:18.522
Each fact sits in a defined catalogue with its source attached.

7
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.891
A couple of answers later, it knows the shape of the plan.

8
00:00:22.351 --> 00:00:27.705
€32,000 saved at AIB, €1,200 a month to put away, a home by next June.

9
00:00:28.192 --> 00:00:31.475
Saoirse offers to remember it, but nothing is kept until she taps.

10
00:00:31.961 --> 00:00:35.069
She can review what Saoirse proposes before she approves it.

11
00:00:35.341 --> 00:00:38.730
The model proposes, the customer commits, the system checks.

12
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.076
The savings are elsewhere, so Saoirse requests access.

13
00:00:42.682 --> 00:00:49.280
With her consent, open banking brings in the available account data, salary arriving, rent going out, savings balance.

14
00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:52.159
The consent has a defined scope and expiry.

15
00:00:52.625 --> 00:00:55.119
She authorises it and the picture fills in.

16
00:00:54.945 --> 00:00:57.817
The consent does not authorise a payment or anything else.

17
00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.422
No statement to upload.

18
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.478
Saoirse reads the permitted data.

19
00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:03.501
Now the money gets put to work.

20
00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.501
This is arithmetic, not opinion.

21
00:01:05.961 --> 00:01:09.918
The lump sum goes into a six month fixed term, ending before she needs it.

22
00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:14.420
€200 a month into mortgage savings account to qualify for the €2,000 bonus.

23
00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.750
The remainder into super savings account at 3%.

24
00:01:17.603 --> 00:01:21.259
Roughly €430 in the first year at the rates shown.

25
00:01:21.733 --> 00:01:24.109
One tap starts three account applications.

26
00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:26.264
The calculation is visible and explainable.

27
00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:29.120
She already banks here, so she signs in.

28
00:01:29.402 --> 00:01:33.051
The prototype uses an email code, not the bank's real identity check.

29
00:01:33.328 --> 00:01:38.059
Existing customer information appears and six fields are reused across three applications.

30
00:01:38.636 --> 00:01:40.096
Here's the important thing to notice.

31
00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:45.361
The super savings account uses the bank's published form, 499 controls.

32
00:01:45.898 --> 00:01:50.902
Saoirse reads the definition, fills what it knows, then asks for the rest in the form's own words.

33
00:01:51.471 --> 00:01:53.615
The €32,000 is still in AIB.

34
00:01:53.975 --> 00:01:58.270
She separately authorises a transfer and the money moves towards her current account here.

35
00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:03.454
Now the bank can monitor her deposit directly without relying on continued access to the other account.

36
00:02:03.866 --> 00:02:06.138
Saoirse will return when it reaches €40,000.

37
00:02:06.328 --> 00:02:09.850
In the console, the fixed term account is opened and the transfer settled.

38
00:02:10.292 --> 00:02:13.790
Back on her phone, Saoirse confirms what's happened.

39
00:02:15.704 --> 00:02:17.846
Now we skip ahead, the months have passed.

40
00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:22.525
The plan stays in the console, along with the milestone the bank agreed to watch.

41
00:02:23.203 --> 00:02:24.662
The balance reaches the target.

42
00:02:24.496 --> 00:02:28.500
A notification lands without exposing financial details.

43
00:02:29.211 --> 00:02:32.895
She opens it and Saoirse picks up exactly where they left off.

44
00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:36.357
The deposit is ready and it's time to revisit the mortgage.

45
00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:38.813
It remembers what she already told it.

46
00:02:39.187 --> 00:02:40.406
Nothing asked twice.

47
00:02:41.817 --> 00:02:43.035
And the other side of the glass.

48
00:02:43.705 --> 00:02:46.448
Every case, every fact and its source.

49
00:02:47.036 --> 00:02:49.928
Linked accounts, transfers, the monitored balance.

50
00:02:50.641 --> 00:02:53.165
Guardrails ahead of the model, not inside it.

51
00:02:53.494 --> 00:02:57.344
Persona controls for style, not policy.

52
00:02:57.555 --> 00:02:59.111
Analytics built from recorded events.

53
00:03:00.047 --> 00:03:03.780
Operations and controls, built in from day one.
